is: The north star says each natural language enters as grammar data (grammar, lexicon, decoder onto a pivot), that every tongue, English included, is a projection column, that natural and programming languages share one shelf, and that all content is stored once as recipes, blueprints and cells. It calls the pivot symbol 'the meaning's one name'.
